// Farming's own random-event roll. Every other skill with a random of its own has one of these; up
// to now Farming had none at all, so a farmer got no random events whatsoever.
//
// HUNG OFF ~farming_xp, which skill_farming/scripts/farming_actions.rs2 already describes as the
// single chokepoint every farming action's experience goes through - the same place cooking and
// crafting hang theirs. That means the roll follows the work rather than the click: raking a patch
// is one roll, and so is harvesting it.
//
// A proc rather than a label like the other skills' dispatchers, because those are jumped to from
// labels and this is called from a proc - and a label cannot be jumped to from inside one.
[proc,macro_randomfarming]
if (~macro_event_allowed = false) {
    return;
}
// One skill-specific event against the general table, weighted the way the other skills weight
// theirs: one slot for the spade, one for each general event. The spade event hands the roll back
// to the general table when there is no spade in reach, so a planting-only farmer is not quietly
// getting fewer randoms than anyone else.
switch_int (random(calc(~macro_event_general_count + 1))) {
    case 0 : ~macro_event_lost_spade_spawn;
    case default : ~macro_event_general_spawn(~macro_event_set_random);
}
